# nomothetic device mode environment variables
# Copy to .env.device: cp .env.device.example .env.device
# .env.device is gitignored — never commit secrets or credentials here.

# =============================================================================
# Deployment (scripts/deploy.sh --mode device)
# =============================================================================

# SSH target for the Raspberry Pi — "user@hostname" or plain IP.
# Required for remote deployment.
# NOMON_PI_HOST=pi@raspberrypi.local
NOMON_PI_HOST=

# Optional path to an SSH private key.
# NOMON_SSH_KEY=~/.ssh/id_ed25519
NOMON_SSH_KEY=

# Optional sudo password for non-interactive remote sudo.
# Leave empty to use interactive sudo prompts.
# NOMON_SUDO_PASS='replace_with_pi_user_password'
NOMON_SUDO_PASS=

# Optional absolute path to the nomothetic repo on the remote Pi.
# Default: ${HOME}/perceptua-nomon/nomothetic
# NOMON_REMOTE_DIR=/home/pi/perceptua-nomon/nomothetic

# Service user / group for systemd service units.
# NOMON_SERVICE_USER=nomon
# NOMON_SERVICE_GROUP=nomon

# =============================================================================
# API Mode
# =============================================================================

NOMON_API_MODE=device

# Path to nomopractic's Wi-Fi Soft AP helper installed on the Pi.
# NOMON_AP_MODE_SCRIPT=/usr/local/bin/ap-mode.sh

# =============================================================================
# Device Authentication
# =============================================================================

# Enable pairing-based authentication for device-mode endpoints.
# NOMON_DEVICE_AUTH=true

# Path to the device JWT signing key on the Pi.
# NOMON_DEVICE_JWT_SECRET_PATH=/var/lib/nomon/device_jwt_secret

# Path to the one-time pairing secret on the Pi.
# NOMON_PAIRING_SECRET_PATH=/var/lib/nomon/pairing_secret

# Directory of registered autonomy-plugin public keys (<plugin>.pub; ADR-019).
# NOMON_PLUGIN_KEY_DIR=/var/lib/nomon/plugin_keys

# =============================================================================
# CORS
# =============================================================================

# Comma-separated allowed origins. Defaults to https://10.0.0.1:8443 if unset.
# NOMON_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8081,https://localhost:8081

# =============================================================================
# TLS Certificate
# =============================================================================

# Additional hostnames/IPs in the self-signed cert's SAN list.
# NOMON_TLS_EXTRA_HOSTS=myhost.example.com,10.0.0.5

# =============================================================================
# Media Storage
# =============================================================================

# NOMON_MEDIA_DIR=~/perceptua-nomon/media

# =============================================================================
# Camera / Stream
# =============================================================================

# Capture resolution, frame rate, encoder, and device index for the camera.
# Shared by still capture, recording, and POST /api/stream/start (all use the
# one API-managed camera instance), plus the standalone debug MJPEG server
# (nomothetic-stream.service). Lower width/height/fps to reduce camera
# CPU/memory load, e.g. when running concurrently with the wake-word
# listener or STT on the same Pi.
# NOM_STREAM_CAMERA=0
# NOM_STREAM_WIDTH=1280
# NOM_STREAM_HEIGHT=720
# NOM_STREAM_FPS=30
# Encoder: "h264" or "mjpeg".
# NOM_STREAM_ENCODER=h264

# =============================================================================
# Audio
# =============================================================================

# Recording and playback devices are auto-detected by PortAudio device name:
# the first input/output device whose name contains the match below
# (case-insensitive; the robot's mic and speaker share a USB PCM2902 codec).
# NOMON_AUDIO_INPUT_NAME=USB
# NOMON_AUDIO_OUTPUT_NAME=USB

# Advanced: force specific PortAudio device indexes. These are PortAudio
# indexes, NOT ALSA card numbers — a wrong input value can segfault
# libportaudio and crash the API, so prefer the name matches above.
# NOMON_AUDIO_INPUT_INDEX=
# NOMON_AUDIO_OUTPUT_INDEX=

# NOMON_AUDIO_VOLUME=80
# Mic capture gain 0-100, applied before recording and wake-word capture. The
# USB PCM2902 is a quiet electret; 80 gives cleaner STT than the old 50. Lower
# it if loud speech crackles (clipping). Reaches the ALSA "Mic"/"Capture"
# controls via the nomopractic set_mic_gain call.
# NOMON_AUDIO_MIC_GAIN=80

# =============================================================================
# MQTT Telemetry
# =============================================================================

# NOMON_MQTT_BROKER=
# NOMON_MQTT_PORT=1883
# NOMON_MQTT_TOPIC=nomon/telemetry
# Separate topic for forwarded autonomy-routine events.
# NOMON_MQTT_AUTONOMY_TOPIC=nomon/autonomy
# NOMON_MQTT_INTERVAL=30

# =============================================================================
# Telemetry Device ID
# =============================================================================

# NOMON_DEVICE_ID=
# NOMON_MODEL=

# =============================================================================
# Autonomy Routines (start/stop endpoints — RoutineManager)
# =============================================================================
# nomothetic launches autonomy routines (autonomon plugins) as subprocesses via
# POST /api/routines/start. These configure how it launches and bounds them.
# A plugin credential (key preferred) is REQUIRED for routine start to work;
# without it, /api/routines/start returns 503. The plugin side is configured in
# autonomon/.env.device.

# Plugin credential the launched routine authenticates with (ADR-019). Path to
# the Ed25519 private key registered with nomothetic; autonomon's deploy writes
# it to /etc/autonomon/plugin.key. Must be readable by the service user.
# NOMON_PLUGIN_KEY=/etc/autonomon/plugin.key

# Static device JWT — fallback when NOMON_PLUGIN_KEY is unset (dev/testing only).
# NOMON_PLUGIN_TOKEN=

# Base URL the launched plugin uses to reach this device's API (self-signed TLS).
# Default: https://127.0.0.1:8443
# NOMON_AUTONOMON_DEVICE_URL=https://127.0.0.1:8443

# Absolute path of the routine catalogue autonomon publishes (routine list, param
# schemas, and the path to its own CLI). nomothetic reads this to list and launch
# routines — no autonomon install is needed in this venv (autonomon ADR-005).
# MUST match NOMON_ROUTINE_CATALOG_PATH in autonomon/.env.device.
NOMON_ROUTINE_CATALOG_PATH=/var/lib/nomon/routine_catalog.json

# Path to the nomon-autonomon console script. Normally taken from the published
# catalogue above (autonomon's own venv); set this only to override it.
# NOMON_AUTONOMON_BIN=

# Max seconds without a heartbeat before a routine is auto-stopped — the
# renewable connection-loss guard. The app (nomotactic) sends heartbeats on an
# interval to keep a routine alive; it stops once they stop arriving.
# NOMON_ROUTINE_HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT_S=120

# Hard ceiling a per-request heartbeat_timeout_s is clamped to, so the guard
# can never be widened arbitrarily from the API.
# NOMON_ROUTINE_HEARTBEAT_CEILING_S=3600

# Optional absolute cap on total runtime regardless of heartbeats. Unset = no
# cap (a routine runs as long as the app maintains contact).
# NOMON_ROUTINE_MAX_DURATION_S=

# Seconds to wait after SIGINT before escalating to SIGKILL when stopping.
# NOMON_ROUTINE_STOP_GRACE_S=5

# ── AI chat-command relay (nomothetic Phase 26) ─────────────────────────────
# POST /api/ai/command runs a Claude tool loop over the same validated device
# operations the app buttons use. Requires the [ai] extra (anthropic SDK) and
# an Anthropic API key.

# Where the user-supplied Anthropic key is persisted (0600, atomic writes) when
# stored via PUT /api/ai/key. A stored key takes precedence over the env var.
# NOMON_AI_API_KEY_PATH=/var/lib/nomon/ai_api_key

# Operator-level fallback key used when no key has been stored via the API.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Anthropic model the relay uses.
# NOMON_AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Per-response token cap (256-8192).
# NOMON_AI_MAX_TOKENS=2048

# Max model<->tool round trips per command (1-25).
# NOMON_AI_MAX_TOOL_ITERATIONS=8

# ── Voice-command transcription (nomothetic Phase 28) ───────────────────────
# POST /api/ai/transcribe converts an uploaded voice clip to text on-device.
# Requires the [stt] extra (vosk), ffmpeg (apt install ffmpeg), and a local
# model (make fetch-stt-model). Missing prerequisites -> 503, never a crash.

# Directory of the unpacked Vosk model.
# NOMON_STT_MODEL_PATH=/var/lib/nomon/stt/vosk-model-small-en-us-0.15

# Upload cap in bytes for one voice clip (~15 s of compressed audio).
# NOMON_STT_MAX_BYTES=2000000

# ── Wake-word voice commands (nomothetic Phase 29, ADR-021) ─────────────────
# The robot listens on its own USB microphone for the catch phrase, chimes,
# captures the spoken command, transcribes it with the local Vosk model, and
# runs it through the same AI command loop as the app's chat bar. Requires the
# [stt] and [audio] extras, the Vosk model (make fetch-stt-model), and an AI
# key. Unset phrase = feature disabled. GET/PUT /api/voice/wake reports and
# updates the listener at runtime (in-memory; this file is the boot config).

# The catch phrase. Every word must exist in the Vosk model's vocabulary —
# out-of-vocabulary words (like "nomon") are silently dropped from the wake
# grammar, so prefer in-vocabulary phrases and tune variants on the device.
# Values with spaces MUST be double-quoted: this file is copied to
# /etc/nomothetic/nomothetic.env, which deploy.sh bash-sources.
# NOMON_WAKE_PHRASE="hey truck"

# Comma-separated alternate spellings that also count as a wake. Use these to
# cover common mishearings of the phrase (tune via PUT /api/voice/wake).
# NOMON_WAKE_PHRASE_VARIANTS="a truck,hey trucks,hey track"

# Capture device selection: by default the listener auto-detects the first
# PortAudio input device whose name contains NOMON_WAKE_INPUT_NAME
# (case-insensitive), falling back to the system default input device.
# NOMON_WAKE_INPUT_NAME=USB

# Chime output device: auto-detected the same way (first PortAudio output
# device matching NOMON_WAKE_OUTPUT_NAME, which defaults to the input name
# match — the speaker usually shares the USB codec). Falls back to the
# system default output, which on HDMI-first Pis is silent.
# NOMON_WAKE_OUTPUT_NAME=USB

# Advanced: force specific PortAudio device indexes. These are PortAudio
# indexes, NOT ALSA card numbers — a wrong input value can segfault
# libportaudio and crash the API, so prefer the name matches above.
# NOMON_WAKE_INPUT_INDEX=
# NOMON_WAKE_OUTPUT_INDEX=

# Seconds to wait for the command to start after the wake chime (1-60).
# NOMON_WAKE_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_S=8

# Hard cap on one utterance before recognition is force-finalised (2-60).
# NOMON_WAKE_MAX_UTTERANCE_S=15

# Follow-up window after a reply — speak again without re-waking; 0 disables
# follow-ups (0-120).
# NOMON_WAKE_FOLLOWUP_WINDOW_S=8

# Timeout for one AI command dispatch (10-300).
# NOMON_WAKE_AI_TIMEOUT_S=120

# Chime volume 0-100 (default: NOMON_AUDIO_VOLUME).
# NOMON_WAKE_CHIME_VOLUME_PCT=80

# RMS energy gate: mic frames quieter than this skip wake decoding entirely,
# keeping idle CPU near zero (0 disables the gate; 0-32767).
# NOMON_WAKE_RMS_THRESHOLD=300

# ── Spoken transcript echo (TTS) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# When a heard command is dispatched, the robot speaks the transcript back
# through the speaker (espeak-ng), concurrently with the AI call, so the echo
# fills the otherwise-silent gap. Requires espeak-ng and ffmpeg (both apt
# packages, see docs/pi_setup.md); when either is missing the spoken echo is
# skipped and the processing chime still plays.

# espeak-ng voice name (see `espeak-ng --voices`).
# NOMON_TTS_VOICE=en

# Speaking rate in words per minute (80-450).
# NOMON_TTS_RATE_WPM=160
